their use of leverage to no more than 50% of the portfolio&#146;s gross asset value
determined as of the date that is the later of the end of the Investment Period
and the date such leverage is incurred. In calculating the 50% limit as well as
the other percentage limitation mentioned below, we will include only the
Fund&#146;s or its subsidiary&#146;s actual percentage interest in any borrowings in
relation to its interest in the gross asset value of the property and not that
of any joint venture partner. Leverage may be in the form of mortgage loans
secured by individual properties in the portfolio or an unsecured credit
facility. Mortgage indebtedness on a particular property may not exceed 60% of
the gross asset value of the property as of the date such indebtedness is
incurred.</FONT></P>

