doctrine established under the U.S. Constitution. The investment income of a
governmental pension plan may not be subject to U.S. federal income taxation by reason of
these provisions (even where such investment income would give rise to UBTI for
a nongovernmental tax exempt entity); however, there are no Treasury
regulations, revenue rulings or judicial decisions which consider this precise
